    "content_type": "text/html",
    "css": ".docxdriver { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.2; color: #111; }\n.docxdriver p, .docxdriver h1, .docxdriver h2, .docxdriver h3, .docxdriver h4, .docxdriver h5, .docxdriver h6 { white-space: pre-wrap; tab-size: 4; min-height: 1em; }\n.docxdriver p { margin: 0 0 .6em; }\n.docxdriver table { border-collapse: collapse; max-width: 100%; }\n.docxdriver td, .docxdriver th { border: 1px solid #aaa; padding: .3em .5em; vertical-align: top; }\n.docxdriver img { max-width: 100%; }\n.docxdriver ins { color: #067a35; text-decoration: underline; }\n.docxdriver del { color: #b32323; text-decoration: line-through; }\n.docxdriver [data-docx-format-change] { background: #fff1b8; }\n.docxdriver [data-docx-field] { background: #f2f4f7; }\n.docxdriver ol, .docxdriver ul { padding-left: 2em; }\n.docxdriver li > p { margin-bottom: .25em; }\n.docxdriver [data-docx-marker]::marker { content: attr(data-docx-marker) \" \"; }\n.docxdriver aside { border-top: 1px solid #ddd; margin-top: 1em; font-size: .9em; }\n.docxdriver [data-docx-break=\"page\"] { break-after: page; }\n.docxdriver [data-docx-break=\"column\"] { break-after: column; }\n.docxdriver header, .docxdriver footer { color: #555; }\n",
    "html": "<section data-docx-section=\"1\" data-docx-page-width-twips=\"12240\" data-docx-page-height-twips=\"15840\" data-docx-column-spacing-twips=\"720\" data-docx-page-number-start=\"2\">\n<header>\n<p data-docx-style=\"Header\" style=\"font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:1;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Application/Control Number: </span><span data-docx-field=\"DOCPROPERTY &quot;FormattedApplicationNumber&quot;\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">18/690,238</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Page </span><span data-docx-field=\"PAGE   \\* MERGEFORMAT\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">1</span></span></p>\n<p data-docx-style=\"Header\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:1;margin-bottom:0pt;\">Art Unit: <span data-docx-field=\"DOCPROPERTY &quot;HeaderArtUnit&quot;\" contenteditable=\"false\">2447</span></p>\n</header>\n<p id=\"521EA745\" data-docx-ord=\"1\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:14pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-align:center;\"><b>DETAILED ACTION</b></p>\n<ol data-docx-list=\"1\" data-docx-level=\"0\" start=\"1\" type=\"1\"><li data-docx-marker=\"1.\"><p id=\"7D03D815\" data-docx-ord=\"2\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" data-docx-number=\"1.\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">The current office action is in response to the communication filed on 3/7/24.</p></li><li data-docx-marker=\"2.\"><p id=\"398FB059\" data-docx-ord=\"3\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" data-docx-number=\"2.\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">The applicant amended claims 1-14 in the Preliminary Amendment received on 3/7/24.</p></li><li data-docx-marker=\"3.\"><p id=\"17858B8D\" data-docx-ord=\"4\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" data-docx-number=\"3.\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">Claims 1-14 are pending.</p></li><li data-docx-marker=\"4.\"><p id=\"794765AE\" data-docx-ord=\"5\" data-docx-style=\"ListParagraph\" data-docx-number=\"4.\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:36pt;\">The Examiner recommends filing a written authorization for Internet communication in response to the present action. Doing so permits the USPTO to communicate with Applicant using Internet email to schedule interviews or discuss other aspects of the application.  Without a written authorization in place, the USPTO cannot respond to Internet correspondence received from Applicant. The preferred method of providing authorization is by filing form PTO/SB/439, available at: https://www.uspto.gov/patent/forms/forms. See MPEP § 502.03 for other methods of providing written authorization.</p></li></ol>\n<p id=\"4314ACA9\" data-docx-ord=\"6\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"0B30B154\" data-docx-ord=\"7\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-align:center;\"><b><i>Notice of Pre-AIA or AIA Status</i></b></p>\n<ol data-docx-list=\"1\" data-docx-level=\"0\" start=\"5\" type=\"1\"><li data-docx-marker=\"5.\"><p id=\"660FA680\" data-docx-ord=\"8\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" data-docx-number=\"5.\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">The present application, filed on or after March 16, 2013, is being examined under the first inventor to file provisions of the AIA.</p></li></ol>\n<p id=\"0173652E\" data-docx-ord=\"9\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"42FD3FAC\" data-docx-ord=\"10\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-align:center;\"><b>Paper Submitted</b></p>\n<ol data-docx-list=\"1\" data-docx-level=\"0\" start=\"6\" type=\"1\"><li data-docx-marker=\"6.\"><p id=\"0880788A\" data-docx-ord=\"11\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" data-docx-number=\"6.\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">It is hereby acknowledged that the following papers have been received and placed of record in the file:</p></li></ol>\n<p id=\"439CF6E9\" data-docx-ord=\"12\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\"><b>Information Disclosure Statement(s)</b> as received on 3/7/24 are considered by the Examiner.</p>\n<p id=\"77B92BFF\" data-docx-ord=\"13\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"15D9D04C\" data-docx-ord=\"14\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-align:center;\"><b><i>Allowable Subject Matter</i></b></p>\n<ol data-docx-list=\"1\" data-docx-level=\"0\" start=\"7\" type=\"1\"><li data-docx-marker=\"7.\"><p id=\"0DA878D9\" data-docx-ord=\"15\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" data-docx-number=\"7.\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">Claims 1-14 would be allowable if the Objections to the Title, Objections to the Specification and Claim Objections listed in the paragraph(s) below are corrected.</p></li><li data-docx-marker=\"8.\"><p id=\"6018B46C\" data-docx-ord=\"16\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" data-docx-number=\"8.\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">As allowable subject matter has been indicated, applicant's reply must either comply with all formal requirements or specifically traverse each requirement not complied with.  See 37 CFR 1.111(b) and MPEP § 707.07(a).</p></li></ol>\n<p id=\"69A809DB\" data-docx-ord=\"17\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"70932BE3\" data-docx-ord=\"18\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-align:center;\"><b><i>Specification</i></b></p>\n<ol data-docx-list=\"1\" data-docx-level=\"0\" start=\"9\" type=\"1\"><li data-docx-marker=\"9.\"><p id=\"5907A637\" data-docx-ord=\"19\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" data-docx-number=\"9.\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">The title of the invention is not descriptive. A new title is required that is clearly indicative of the invention to which the claims are directed.</p></li><li data-docx-marker=\"10.\"><p id=\"538B16B9\" data-docx-ord=\"20\" data-docx-style=\"ListParagraph\" data-docx-number=\"10.\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:36pt;\">The disclosure is objected to because of the following informalities:</p></li><li data-docx-marker=\"11.\"><p id=\"19F3A521\" data-docx-ord=\"21\" data-docx-style=\"ListParagraph\" data-docx-number=\"11.\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:36pt;\">Typically abbreviations/acronyms are used after an expansion is provided to the abbreviations/acronyms. However, in the Specification, “IT,” “Tcpdump,” “Mb/sec,” “IP,” “FPGA,” “I/O,” “CPU,” “TCP,” “IPsec,” “GRE,” “L2TP,” “TLS,” “URL,” “RAM,” “NIC,” “EPROM,” “VLAN,” “VxLAN,” “MPLS,” “DNS,” “SSH,” “DHCP,” “UDP,” “HTTP,” “LDAP,” “RDP,” “ID,” “Gbps,” etc. are used before they are expanded. It is suggested to use expansions before using their abbreviations/acronyms. Appropriate correction is required.</p></li></ol>\n<p id=\"2ECE71A5\" data-docx-ord=\"22\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"40EA9BB0\" data-docx-ord=\"23\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-align:center;\"><b><i>Claim Objections</i></b></p>\n<ol data-docx-list=\"1\" data-docx-level=\"0\" start=\"12\" type=\"1\"><li data-docx-marker=\"12.\"><p id=\"0CBD9616\" data-docx-ord=\"24\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" data-docx-number=\"12.\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">Claims 1-14 are objected to because the claim language is replete with antecedent basis, grammatical and idiomatic errors. The examiner suggests the following amendments to claims 1-14 in order to place the application in condition for allowance:</p></li><li data-docx-marker=\"13.\"><p id=\"6D829064\" data-docx-ord=\"25\" data-docx-style=\"ListParagraph\" data-docx-number=\"13.\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:36pt;\">Replace all prior versions, and listings, of claims in the application as follows:</p></li></ol>\n<p id=\"57CC88CF\" data-docx-ord=\"26\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"686B5CDA\" data-docx-ord=\"27\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">1 . A method of processing of a data stream comprising batches of packets, each batch of packets defined by a protocol chain of communication protocols associated with at least one session, comprising:</p>\n<p id=\"603D663B\" data-docx-ord=\"28\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">receiving a plurality of batches of data packets via a communication channel and storing said plurality of batches of data packets in a temporary memory;</p>\n<p id=\"66648134\" data-docx-ord=\"29\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">performing, for each batch of data packets of the plurality of batches of data packets, a protocol analysis (DAPD) enabling the communication protocols in the protocol chain to be identified, and validating the at least one session associated with the protocol chain based on the identification of the protocol chain being complete;</p>\n<p id=\"0D544475\" data-docx-ord=\"30\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">determining at least one digital session fingerprint (HS) associated with the identified protocol chain (PID) of the at least one session validated during the validation step,</p>\n<p id=\"7E7A62BB\" data-docx-ord=\"31\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">storing said determined digital session fingerprint(s) (HS) in at least one hash table (TH), and saving a list (LM) of metadata (MPID) associated with the identified communication protocols (PID) of the protocol chain of the at least one validated session in a knowledge database (BDDS);</p>\n<p id=\"04E22F65\" data-docx-ord=\"32\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">generating at least one trigger based on the protocol analysis results (DAPD), wherein activation of the at least one trigger is indicative of a match between at least one rule for identifying target metadata (MC) and the metadata (MPID) associated with the identified communication protocols (PID), the list (LM) is saved in the knowledge database (BDDS);</p>\n<p id=\"02141B1D\" data-docx-ord=\"33\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">analysing the metadata (MPID) associated with the identified communication protocols (PID) of a particular batch of data packets of the at least one validated session, stored in the temporary memory, against the saved list (LM) of metadata (MPID) associated with the identified communication protocols (PID) in the knowledge database (BDDS), and checking whether the metadata (MPID) associated with the identified communication protocols (PID) comply with the at least one trigger’s rule for identifying the target metadata (MC);</p>\n<p id=\"0AFBFC83\" data-docx-ord=\"34\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">determining the metadata comply with the at least one trigger’s rule for identifying the target metadata (MC);</p>\n<p id=\"54FE9910\" data-docx-ord=\"35\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">activating the at least one trigger and assigning a save status (SV) to the at least one digital session fingerprint (HS) of the at least one validated session; and</p>\n<p id=\"441638B2\" data-docx-ord=\"36\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">emptying the temporary memory of each batch of data packets of the plurality of batches of data packets for which the at least one digital session fingerprint does not have a save status (SV), and saving on a storage memory for subsequent processing all data packets for which the at least one associated digital session fingerprint (HS) has a save status (SV).</p>\n<p id=\"02BDEBB4\" data-docx-ord=\"37\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"43758B2F\" data-docx-ord=\"38\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">2 . The method according to claim 1, wherein the step of activation of the at least one trigger further comprises updating the at least one hash table (TH) saved following the step of saving the at least one digital session fingerprint (HS), by assigning the save status (SV) to the at least one digital session fingerprint (HS).</p>\n<p id=\"2B4241B2\" data-docx-ord=\"39\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"0360D849\" data-docx-ord=\"40\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">3 . The method according to claim 1, wherein the step of emptying the temporary memory further comprises consulting the at least one hash table (TH) to check whether one of the at least one digital session fingerprint (HS) associated with the particular batch of data packets subject to emptying has the save status (SV).</p>\n<p id=\"64BD9282\" data-docx-ord=\"41\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"40355E2C\" data-docx-ord=\"42\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">4 . The method according to claim 1, wherein the step of analysis of the metadata associated with the identified communication protocols (PID) of the particular batch of data packets of the at least one validated session further comprises analysing the metadata associated with attached content (MP) of the protocol chain of the at least one validated session, wherein the analysing the metadata associated with the attached content (MP) is based on the at least one trigger’s rule for identifying the target metadata (MC) comprising the target metadata (MC) in relation to the attached content (MP).</p>\n<p id=\"2FBF0F18\" data-docx-ord=\"43\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"47F0CFD9\" data-docx-ord=\"44\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">5 . The method according to claim 1, wherein the at least one trigger processes and applies a dynamic list of rules for identifying the target metadata (MC).</p>\n<p id=\"1CCED26A\" data-docx-ord=\"45\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"47498066\" data-docx-ord=\"46\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">6 . The method according to claim 1, wherein the target metadata (MC) of identification rules of the at least one trigger belong to a group formed by native metadata and other metadata calculated from selected mathematical formulae.</p>\n<p id=\"67E6BDC5\" data-docx-ord=\"47\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"03E156CB\" data-docx-ord=\"48\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">7 . The method according to claim 1, wherein the target metadata (MC) are representative of selected network parameters belonging to a group formed by destination internet protocol (IP), source IP, destination port, source port, protocol, IP address, port, quality of service (QoS) parameters, network tag, session volume, packet size, number of retries, version, encryption algorithm type and version, encryption type, Computer Emergency Response Team (CERT) certificate, Server Name Indication (SNI) value, packet size, returned IP, error flag, domain name, client version, server version, encryption algorithm version, compression algorithm, timestamp, IP version, hostname, lease-time, Uniform Resource Locator (URL), user agent, number of bytes of content attached, content type, status code, cookie header, client name, request service, error code value, request type, protocol value, response timestamp, privilege level, keyboard type and language, product identification, screen size, or any similar specific metadata extracted from the communication protocols in one or more data packets of the at least one validated session, similar specific metadata extracted from content attached to the one or more data packets of the at least one validated session.</p>\n<p id=\"69A12126\" data-docx-ord=\"49\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"2E1B7F34\" data-docx-ord=\"50\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">8 . The method according to claim 1, wherein the step of protocol analysis (DAPD) and the step of analysing the metadata of the particular batch of data packets of the at least one validated session (MPID) are carried out on data packets of layer 2 to layer 7 of the Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) model.</p>\n<p id=\"6AABC0B7\" data-docx-ord=\"51\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"29356805\" data-docx-ord=\"52\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">9 . A system for processing of a data stream comprising batches of packets, each batch of packets defined by a protocol chain of communication protocols associated with at least one session, comprising:</p>\n<p id=\"26806CE3\" data-docx-ord=\"53\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">network interface (NIC) configured to receive the data stream from a communication channel;</p>\n<p id=\"43AE95DD\" data-docx-ord=\"54\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">a processor comprising at least one processing core for processing a predetermined number of data packets per minute (ppm);</p>\n<p id=\"628EACC9\" data-docx-ord=\"55\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">a temporary memory, coupled to the processor, storing a plurality of batches of data packets from the network interface (NIC);</p>\n<p id=\"345F29C4\" data-docx-ord=\"56\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">a protocol analysis engine executed on the at least one processing core, wherein the protocol analysis engine is configured to:</p>\n<p id=\"2034898D\" data-docx-ord=\"57\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">receive the plurality of batches of data packets within a predetermined time via the communication channel;</p>\n<p id=\"0DF1FF9E\" data-docx-ord=\"58\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">perform, for each batch of data packets of the plurality of batches of data packets, a protocol analysis (DAPD) enabling the communication protocols in the protocol chain to be identified, and validating at least one associated session;</p>\n<p id=\"184261A4\" data-docx-ord=\"59\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">determine at least one digital session fingerprint (HS) associated with the identified protocol chain (PID) of the validated at least one associated session, and</p>\n<p id=\"2CA64E4A\" data-docx-ord=\"60\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">store said determined digital session fingerprint (HS) in at least one hash table (TH), and save a list (LM) of metadata (MPID) associated with the identified communication protocols (PID) of the protocol chain of the validated at least one associated session in a knowledge database (BDDS);</p>\n<p id=\"04C0CE60\" data-docx-ord=\"61\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">a monitoring engine executed on the at least one processing core, wherein the monitoring engine performs:</p>\n<p id=\"28E7D503\" data-docx-ord=\"62\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">generating at least one trigger based on the protocol analysis results (DAPD), wherein activation of the at least one trigger is indicative of a match between at least one rule for identifying target metadata (MC) and the list (LM) of metadata (MPID) associated with the identified communication protocols (PID) of the protocol chain of the validated at least one associated session;</p>\n<p id=\"18623F08\" data-docx-ord=\"63\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">analysing the metadata of a particular batch of data packets of the validated at least one associated session, stored in the temporary memory, against the saved list (LM) of metadata (MPID) associated with the identified communication protocols (PID) in the knowledge database (BDDS), and checking whether the metadata (MPID) associated with the identified communication protocols (PID) comply with the at least one trigger’s rule for identifying the target metadata (MC);</p>\n<p id=\"10A73718\" data-docx-ord=\"64\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">determining the metadata comply with the at least one trigger’s rule for identifying the target metadata (MC);</p>\n<p id=\"12FC5D42\" data-docx-ord=\"65\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">activating the at least one trigger and assigning a save status (SV) to at least one digital session fingerprint (HS) of the validated at least one associated session; and</p>\n<p id=\"6535512E\" data-docx-ord=\"66\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">emptying the temporary memory for each batch of data packets of the plurality of batches of data packets for which the at least one digital session fingerprint(s) (HS) do not have a save status (SV); and</p>\n<p id=\"5B92D06B\" data-docx-ord=\"67\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">a storage memory coupled to the processor saving, for subsequent processing, all data packets for which the at least one associated digital session fingerprint (HS) has a save status (SV).</p>\n<p id=\"474C3D8D\" data-docx-ord=\"68\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"6FDC17AC\" data-docx-ord=\"69\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">10 . The system according to claim 9, wherein the monitoring engine is configured to update the at least one hash table (TH) saved following the step of saving the at least one digital session fingerprint (HS), by assigning the save status (SV) to the at least one digital session fingerprint (HS) based on activation of the at least one trigger.</p>\n<p id=\"36BB1449\" data-docx-ord=\"70\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"7D2273EF\" data-docx-ord=\"71\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">11 . The system according to claim 9, wherein the monitoring engine is configured to consult the at least one hash table (TH) and check whether the at least one digital session fingerprint (HS) associated with the particular batch of data packets of the validated at least one associated session has a save status (SV).</p>\n<p id=\"78122083\" data-docx-ord=\"72\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"52A7BE72\" data-docx-ord=\"73\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">12 . The system according to claim 9, wherein the monitoring engine is configured to analyse the metadata associated with attached content (MP) of the protocol chain of the validated at least one associated session during the analysis of the metadata (MPID) associated with the identified communication protocols (PID) of the particular batch of data packets of the validated at least one associated session, wherein the analysing the metadata associated with the attached content (MP) is based on the at least one trigger’s rule for identifying the target metadata (MC) comprising the target metadata (MC) in relation to the attached content (MP).</p>\n<p id=\"2FB59D32\" data-docx-ord=\"74\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"22E5A1D7\" data-docx-ord=\"75\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">13 . The system according to claim 9, wherein the temporary memory is gradually emptied based on usage of an associated Random Access Memory (RAM) being between 95% and 98%.</p>\n<p id=\"19A349F9\" data-docx-ord=\"76\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"1167E226\" data-docx-ord=\"77\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">14 . The system according to claim 9, wherein the temporary memory is emptied chronologically by deleting oldest data packets at a chosen emptying rate.</p>\n<p id=\"4D6D43B5\" data-docx-ord=\"78\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"73CB6665\" data-docx-ord=\"79\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-align:center;text-indent:36pt;\"><b><i>Conclusion</i></b></p>\n<ol data-docx-list=\"1\" data-docx-level=\"0\" start=\"14\" type=\"1\"><li data-docx-marker=\"14.\"><p id=\"5D242341\" data-docx-ord=\"80\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" data-docx-number=\"14.\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">The prior art made of record and not relied upon is considered pertinent to applicant’s disclosure:</p></li></ol><ul data-docx-list=\"2\" data-docx-level=\"0\"><li data-docx-marker=\"•\"><p id=\"4E696A7A\" data-docx-ord=\"81\" data-docx-style=\"ListParagraph\" data-docx-number=\"•\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:36pt;\">Knott. US 2013/0232137. Discloses analyzing data packets based on content and metadata.</p></li><li data-docx-marker=\"•\"><p id=\"3D269972\" data-docx-ord=\"82\" data-docx-style=\"ListParagraph\" data-docx-number=\"•\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:36pt;\">Watson et al. US 2021/0385138. Discloses monitoring and capturing packets sent over a network.</p></li><li data-docx-marker=\"•\"><p id=\"0CD97D10\" data-docx-ord=\"83\" data-docx-style=\"ListParagraph\" data-docx-number=\"•\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:36pt;\">Hsiao et al. US 2015/0293954. Discloses grouping and managing event streams generated from captured network data.</p></li><li data-docx-marker=\"•\"><p id=\"0E9F8FB4\" data-docx-ord=\"84\" data-docx-style=\"ListParagraph\" data-docx-number=\"•\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:36pt;\">Farmer et al. US 2016/0112287. Discloses storage, recovery, and analysis of network traffic data.</p></li><li data-docx-marker=\"•\"><p id=\"234D5083\" data-docx-ord=\"85\" data-docx-style=\"ListParagraph\" data-docx-number=\"•\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:36pt;\">Maher et al. US 2003/0227917. Discloses enabling trap and trace of internet protocol communications.</p></li></ul>\n<p id=\"1A58AB68\" data-docx-ord=\"86\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<ol data-docx-list=\"1\" data-docx-level=\"0\" start=\"15\" type=\"1\"><li data-docx-marker=\"15.\"><p id=\"56B48567\" data-docx-ord=\"87\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" data-docx-number=\"15.\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;\">Any inquiry concerning this communication or earlier communications from the examiner should be directed to <span data-docx-field=\"FILLIN &quot;Enter examiner's name&quot; \\* MERGEFORMAT\" contenteditable=\"false\">Johnny B Aguiar</span> whose telephone number is <span data-docx-field=\"FILLIN &quot;Phone number&quot; \\* MERGEFORMAT\" contenteditable=\"false\">(571)272-3563</span>. The examiner can normally be reached on <span data-docx-field=\"FILLIN &quot;Work schedule?&quot; \\* MERGEFORMAT\" contenteditable=\"false\">Monday to Friday 7:30 am - 5:30 pm EST</span>.</p></li></ol>\n<p id=\"666EAB57\" data-docx-ord=\"88\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">Examiner interviews are available via telephone, in-person, and video conferencing using a USPTO supplied web-based collaboration tool. To schedule an interview, applicant is encouraged to use the USPTO Automated Interview Request (AIR) at http://www.uspto.gov/interviewpractice.</p>\n<p id=\"3EB00A2A\" data-docx-ord=\"89\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">If attempts to reach the examiner by telephone are unsuccessful, the examiner’s supervisor, <span data-docx-field=\"FILLIN &quot;SPE Name?&quot; \\* MERGEFORMAT\" contenteditable=\"false\">Joon Hwang</span> can be reached on <span data-docx-field=\"FILLIN &quot;SPE Phone?&quot; \\* MERGEFORMAT\" contenteditable=\"false\">(571) 272-4036</span>.  The fax phone number for the organization where this application or proceeding is assigned is 571-273-8300.</p>\n<p id=\"0282B3C5\" data-docx-ord=\"90\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:2;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">Information regarding the status of an application may be obtained from the Patent Application Information Retrieval (PAIR) system.  Status information for published applications may be obtained from either Private PAIR or Public PAIR.  Status information for unpublished applications is available through Private PAIR only.  For more information about the PAIR system, see http://pair-direct.uspto.gov. Should you have questions on access to the Private PAIR system, contact the Electronic Business Center (EBC) at 866-217-9197 (toll-free). If you would like assistance from a USPTO Customer Service Representative or access to the automated information system, call 800-786-9199 (IN USA OR CANADA) or 571-272-1000.</p>\n<p id=\"6B373D1E\" data-docx-ord=\"91\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"line-height:1.0791666666666666;margin-bottom:0pt;\"></p>\n<p id=\"41309CB7\" data-docx-ord=\"92\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:1;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">/JOHNNY B AGUIAR/</p>\n<p id=\"7AE9EB8F\" data-docx-ord=\"93\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:1;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">Primary Examiner, Art Unit 2447</p>\n<p id=\"46637D4C\" data-docx-ord=\"94\" data-docx-style=\"Normal\" style=\"color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:12pt;line-height:1;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:36pt;\">June 5, 2025</p>\n</section>",
